course: dictionary
lesson: 10299
title: Tough: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: The word tough can mean different things, so the words around it give the clues. «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» Here tough means strong and not easily broken, because the recorders must survive a crash.
explain: «Maddie's ball gets chewed to shreds by the neighbour's Staffie. «Tough luck, love.»» Here tough means too bad. The mum says it rather rudely, and it is not about strength at all. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Tough can also mean hard to do, or strict and firm. «Tough rules» are rules that are not easily bent. «It is so tough that ginkgos near the Hiroshima bomb sprouted again» means the tree is strong enough to survive, which is a big clue that tough means strong here.
fact: Tough means strong and not easily broken, cut or damaged, as in «tough boots».
fact: Tough also means hard to do, as in «a tough test».
fact: A tough person is strong in body or mind and can deal with pain or problems.
fact: «Tough luck» is said, rather rudely, to mean «too bad».
fact: «Tough it out» means keep going, even when things are hard.
exercise: «She wore tough boots for the rocky hike.» What does tough mean here? | Hard to do | Wet and cold | *Strong and not easily broken | Strict and firm
exercise: Maddie's mum says, «Tough luck, love.» What does she mean? | Lucky day | Well done, you won | Please come here quickly | *Too bad
exercise: In PE the teacher shouts, «Tough it out, keep running!» What does tough it out mean? | Shout as loudly as you can | Stop and sit down | Change into new shoes | *Keep going even when it is hard
test: «The rules at the club were tough and strict.» What does tough mean here? | *Strict and firm | Quick and light | Happy and friendly | Soft and easy to chew
test: Which word fits best? «The steak was so ___ that I could hardly chew it.» | Soft | Sweet | Warm | *Tough
exam: Which meaning fits a tough character in a story who does not give up? | Easily upset and quick to cry | Always sleepy and slow | Very small and quiet | *Strong in body or mind, and able to deal with problems
